{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "72043f43-5dcc-4e00-9478-e11ef1757894",
    "name": "Raffle System API",
    "description": "Raffle ticket API (Bun + Elysia + Difunkt + SQLite).\n\nRun the whole collection top to bottom against a freshly seeded server:\n\n    bun install && bun run dev\n\nEvery request carries assertions, so a full run is an end-to-end check of the API, including the three guarantees that matter most:\n\n1. a raffle never sells more tickets than exist;\n2. a retried purchase is never charged twice;\n3. ticket numbers are unique within a raffle.\n\nThe `3. Tickets` folder proves (2) interactively: it buys, retries with the same `Idempotency-Key`, and then checks the balance moved exactly once.\n\nCollection-level auth is a bearer token captured by `1. Auth > Log in as Alice`. Requests that must be anonymous override it to `No Auth`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
